# Review routing. A pull request that touches a path here requests review from
# the listed owner, and branch protection requires that review before merge.
#
# Two roles. The repository owner reviews everything that carries a safety
# property or defines what the repository claims. The macOS contributor owns
# the POSIX layer - they run it daily, and their review of a change there is
# worth more than the owner's. Both are listed on the paths where a change to
# one platform's layer could change the other's behaviour.
#
# The macOS contributor (@dfeteau) co-owns the POSIX layer.

# Default: everything.
*                                              @jordanmrash

# Safety properties. Owner-only, always.
/Startup/CommandBridge/                        @jordanmrash
/Startup/FlowBridge/                           @jordanmrash
/scripts/public_scan.py                        @jordanmrash
/scripts/exec_bridge_selftest.py               @jordanmrash
/SECURITY.md                                   @jordanmrash

# What the repository claims about itself and its facts.
/docs/bridge-facts.json                        @jordanmrash
/scripts/facts_check.py                        @jordanmrash
/scripts/release_check.py                      @jordanmrash
/AGENTS.md                                     @jordanmrash
/CoworkConfig/Skills/self-improvement/         @jordanmrash

# The POSIX layer. Either owner's review satisfies the requirement.
/Startup/posix/                                @jordanmrash @dfeteau
/docs/setup-macos.md                           @jordanmrash @dfeteau
/docs/evidence/                                @jordanmrash @dfeteau